{"relationshipsSections":[{"type":"inheritsFrom","kind":"relationships","identifiers":["doc:\/\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/s16SendableMetatypeP","doc:\/\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/17SwiftSyntaxMacros13AttachedMacroP","doc:\/\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/17SwiftSyntaxMacros5MacroP","doc:\/\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/17SwiftSyntaxMacros9PeerMacroP"],"title":"Inherits From"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A macro that turns the declaration it’s attached to into a linker-set record of one kind."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"LinkerSetMacro"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"PeerMacro","preciseIdentifier":"s:17SwiftSyntaxMacros9PeerMacroP"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A client declares its own macro by conforming a type in its compiler plugin and returning","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"its kind; the expansion is shared:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["import LinkerSetsMacroSupport","import SwiftCompilerPlugin","","@main","struct RoutesPlugin: CompilerPlugin {","    let providingMacros: [any Macro.Type] = [RouteMacro.self]","}","","public enum RouteMacro: LinkerSetMacro {","    public static func kind(of attribute: AttributeSyntax) -> UInt32 { 0x726F_7574 }","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The expansion is a private "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@used"},{"type":"text","text":" peer, placed with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@section"},{"type":"text","text":" in the section LinkerSets"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"owns, whose accessor produces the declaration’s value:"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"a static property’s or a global variable’s value;"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"a static or free function, as a value of its function type;"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"a struct, enum, class or actor, as its metatype: ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"any P.Type"},{"text":" when","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/documentation\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/LinkerSetMacro\/requiredConformance(of:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" names a protocol ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"P"},{"text":", which the type must then conform to or the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"expansion doesn’t compile, and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Any.Type"},{"text":" otherwise.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A function isolated to the main actor, by its own ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@MainActor"},{"text":" or its type’s or extension’s,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is stored as its isolated type (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@MainActor () -> Void"},{"text":"), read with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"LinkerSet<@MainActor () -> Void>"},{"text":" and called on the main actor. A property isolated to the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"main actor is refused, since the record’s nonisolated accessor can’t read it: one marked","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@MainActor"},{"text":", or a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"var"},{"text":" of a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@MainActor"},{"text":" type. Only a written ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@MainActor"},{"text":" is seen. A custom","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"global actor’s attribute, and isolation a type inherits from a protocol it conforms to, can’t","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"be seen in the syntax, so a member isolated that way fails to compile inside the expansion.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"It diagnoses anything else, each with a message of its own: generic functions and types,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"members of generic types, instance members, protocol requirements, declarations inside a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"function, closure or accessor, and a kind that isn’t a 32-bit literal other than 0.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Before swift-syntax 600 a macro can’t see its lexical context. There a type it registers must"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"be declared at file scope, and the compiler, not the macro, refuses a local declaration or a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"member of a generic type, with an error in the expansion."}]}]}],"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/documentation\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport"]]},"sections":[],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Protocol","remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/LinkerSets\/blob\/main\/Sources\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/LinkerSetMacro.swift#L48","fileName":"LinkerSetMacro.swift"},"symbolKind":"protocol","externalID":"s:22LinkerSetsMacroSupport0a3SetC0P","role":"symbol","title":"LinkerSetMacro","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"LinkerSetMacro","kind":"identifier"}],"modules":[{"name":"LinkerSetsMacroSupport"}],"fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"LinkerSetMacro","kind":"identifier"}]},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/linkersetsmacrosupport\/linkersetmacro"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"identifier":{"url":